@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+# M1 C1.1 — response to review round 3
+
+Review: `reviews/M1-C1.1-r3.md` (verdict block; 0 P0, 3 P1, 3 P2), merged as `a551cd0`. Fixes: `386f032`.
+Builder: Claude Opus 5.5. Date: 2026-10-18.
+
+**All six findings are fixed now; none is ticketed, disputed or deferred.** The three P2s were small, so none is
+marked expected-fail. The three register rows the reviewer could not verify (388, 392, 394) are closed, and so are
+rows 56 and 57, which R3-01 had downgraded.
+
+All 8 new round-3 regressions pass, and all 105 earlier review tests still pass, including the 10 000-case
+`c11_r3_random` property. The review's tickets #1–#3 (R3-04/05/06) are resolved by this commit; I have not closed
+the GitHub issues and leave that to the orchestrator.
+
+## Reviewer-owned test edits this round
+
+Each edit reflects the C11-R3-02 ruling: "remove the stateless `invert` from the public API … `invert_against` is the
+only inversion; update … every caller. The reviewer's test must pass." Removing the function means every reviewer
+test that called it must call `invert_against` with its pre-state; otherwise the test no longer compiles. Every
+edited line carries a comment naming the ruling, and every assertion is unchanged.
+
+| # | File:line (after the edit) | Edit |
+|---|---|---|
+| 6 | `crates/model/tests/c11_r1_adversarial.rs:260–267` (`add_over_existing_object_property_is_invertible`) | `change::invert(&patch)` → `change::invert_against(&a, &patch).unwrap()` |
+| 7 | `crates/model/tests/c11_r1_adversarial.rs:275–282` (`move_over_existing_object_property_is_invertible`) | same; `rustfmt` wrapped the unchanged assertion over four lines |
+| 8 | `crates/model/tests/c11_r2_adversarial.rs:235–238` (opaque patch round trip) | same, against `a` |
+| 9 | `crates/model/tests/c11_r2_adversarial.rs:308–310` (elided operations) | `apply(&value, &invert(&[p])).is_err()` → `invert_against(&value, &[p]).is_err()`: inverting an elided operation still must fail |
+| 10 | `crates/model/tests/c11_r3_adversarial.rs:143–146` (`resolved_stateless_move_inverse_does_not_shift_numeric_object_keys`) | `change::invert(&patch)` → `change::invert_against(&before, &patch).unwrap()`; the assertion and its message are unchanged, and the test passes |
+
+Edits 1–5 (rounds 1–2) were accepted in round 3. No other reviewer-owned test file was touched: `git diff` against
+`a551cd0` shows changes only in these three files and only at these call sites. Builder-owned callers were updated
+the same way: `conformance.rs`, `properties.rs` and the `change.rs` unit tests.
+
+## P1
+
+### C11-R3-01 — opaque text received mouth-track range validation — **fixed** (`386f032`)
+
+- **Diff side.** `diff_json` emits a mouth range operation only for the declared field: a `SoundPlacement` own view's
+  `/mouthTrack/mouths` (`change.rs:479`), next to the existing `Element` `/exposure` rule. The same suffix inside
+  `meta`/`ext` is diffed as an ordinary value.
+- **Apply side.** A range operation on any other path, or under a `meta`/`ext` token, is refused with
+  `arg.invalid` (`change.rs:615`). So a range-shaped patch can never range-validate opaque data either: opaque values
+  are replaced wholesale.
+
+Tests: M3 `opaque_mouth_track_lookalikes_are_ordinary_json_changes` (both namespaces) and the unit test
+`range_operations_apply_only_to_declared_fields`.
+
+### C11-R3-02 — the stateless `invert` corrupted numeric object members — **fixed by removal** (`386f032`)
+
+`change::invert(patch)` and its path-shift helper are removed from the public API. `apply_with_inverse` and
+`invert_against` (`change.rs:523,531`) are the only inversion. The module docs, ADR-0010 §4, ADR-0011 §7, the
+handoff and traceability now say so, and every caller is updated (edits above and the builder-owned callers). The
+reviewer's test passes: inverting against the pre-state knows `/a` is an object, so nothing shifts.
+
+### C11-R3-03 — zero-count exposure runs deleted a frame — **fixed** (`386f032`)
+
+- **Patch boundary.** `expand_runs` (`change.rs:379`) refuses any run with count 0. A range replace whose `value`
+  or `oldValue` contains one is therefore `arg.invalid`, raised before anything is mutated. Totals stay bounded, and
+  window consistency (`to`, current content) was already checked.
+- **Model check.** `Element` reports every zero-count run as `runCount` (`validate.rs:838`), even for values built
+  through the public `Deserialize`.
+
+Tests: M3 `zero_length_exposure_runs_are_invalid_range_payloads`, the unit tests
+`range_replace_checks_types_window_and_bounds` (three zero-run payloads) and
+`zero_count_exposure_runs_are_reported_by_the_model_check`.
+
+## P2 (fixed now; no tickets)
+
+### C11-R3-04 — property discovery narrowed the value domain — **fixed** (`386f032`)
+
+`property_schema` (`schema.rs:649`) still collects every candidate down the path, but only the property's own
+declaration contributes validation keywords, kept whole: it follows only its `$ref` chain, so `anyOf`/`oneOf` stay
+intact. Later candidates from kind rules contribute annotations only.
+
+Results: `/colourId` accepts an ID and `null`; `/tip` accepts all four tips; nested conditional paths and `$ref`
+annotations still resolve. Tests: M3 `property_schema_preserves_nullable_value_domains`,
+`property_schema_preserves_every_enum_alternative`, and `property_schema_nested_conditionals_and_ref_annotations_survive`
+(still green).
+
+### C11-R3-05 — mixed double/wide-integer alternatives rejected — **fixed** (`386f032`)
+
+`wireJson.ts`: an `anyOf`/`oneOf` alternative applies when the container validates as parsed, or after coercion
+under that alternative alone. Coercing under one alternative converts its large doubles and keeps its wide
+integers. Both T3 cases pass: the three-branch `mixed` value and the generated Element inside `anyOf(Element,
+null)` with `rev = 9007199254740997n`, which is not rounded. The reviewer's 10 MB validation measured 1 075 ms
+(`measurements/ts-10mb-drawing-node.log`).
+
+### C11-R3-06 — anonymous declarations without `x-since` — **fixed** (`386f032`)
+
+The annotation pass (`schema.rs:356`) now descends into anonymous declarations: object alternatives of
+`anyOf`/`oneOf`/`allOf`, inline objects under properties, items, prefix items and map values. It does not descend
+into `if`/`then`/`else` predicates. `DynamicParam`'s `value` and `keyframes` carry `x-since: "1.0"`. Test: M3
+`anonymous_variant_property_declarations_have_since`.
+
+## Register rows
+
+| Stable row | Requirement | R3 status | Now | Source | Test |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 388 | change sets, inversion, range edits (10 §2.6) | divergent | implemented | `change.rs:379` (run counts), `:479` (declared mouth slot), `:523/:531` (only inversion), `:615` (range fields) | M3 `resolved_stateless_move_inverse_…`, `zero_length_exposure_runs_…`; `c11_r3_random::ten_thousand_rfc6902_sequences_apply_and_invert` |
+| 392 | property `x-since` / `readOnly` (10 §2.8) | divergent | implemented | `schema.rs:356` | M3 `anonymous_variant_property_declarations_have_since`; M2 `every_schema_property_has_since_and_envelope_type_is_readonly` |
+| 394 | property-schema lookup (10 §10.2) | divergent | implemented | `schema.rs:649` | M3 `property_schema_preserves_nullable_value_domains`, `property_schema_preserves_every_enum_alternative`, `property_schema_nested_conditionals_and_ref_annotations_survive` |
+| 56 / 57 | `meta` never interpreted / `ext` preserved (10 §2.2) | divergent (R3-01) | implemented | `change.rs:479`, `:615` | M3 `opaque_mouth_track_lookalikes_are_ordinary_json_changes` |
+
+None is disputed.
+
+## Gates and evidence
+
+Local (Windows 11). Raw logs are in `reviews/evidence/M1-C1.1-r3-response/gates/`, with SHA-256 hashes in
+`receipt.json`:
+
+- `cargo fmt --check`;
+- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -D warnings`, and the diagnostics variant;
+- `cargo test --workspace --locked`: **278 passed**, 1 standing SIMD-policy ignore;
+- `tt-desktop` tests with diagnostics;
+- `cargo deny --locked check`;
+- `pnpm lint`, `typecheck`, `test` (**Vitest 39 files, 326 passed; Node 9 passed**), `format:check`,
+  `licenses:check`;
+- `node --test scripts/check-npm-licenses.test.mjs` (9 passed);
+- both front-end builds (dist check ok);
+- headless release build, `--selftest` twice (identical, all ok), dependency guard;
+- `c03-r1-tooling.py`;
+- `c11-r2-review-policy.py` on the committed tree `386f032`: 2 passed (`gates/review-policy-at-386f032.log`).
+
+CI: run **39176265687** on `cd011e3` (fixes + this response), all 8 jobs green.
